# svGolf PINNED scoring flow for CLOCKED designs, stage 2 of 2: SYNTHESIS AND
# MEASUREMENT (Yosys + ABC). The combinational flow (svgolf.ys) with `-nofsm`
# on `synth`, ONE line, `dfflegalize`, after it, and `-purge` on the last
# `opt_clean`. Do not edit: a change here
# is a change to every sequential score. score.py (`--seq`) fills the @NAME@ placeholders and records
# this file's sha256 (`script_sha256`) in every result; the combinational flow,
# its file and its hashes are untouched.
#
#   @RTLIL@    the canonical RTLIL from stage 1 (canon.ys, shared)
#   @TOP@      the task's top module
#   @STAT@     output file for `stat -json` (cell counts by type)
#   @LTP@      output file for `ltp -noff` (longest topological path)
#   @NETLIST@  output file: the scored netlist (gates and $_DFF_P_ flops)
#
# `-nofsm` (decided 2026-11-06): `synth` skips its `fsm` pass and nothing
# else (Yosys 0.53, `help synth`: "fsm (unless -nofsm)"). That pass re-encodes
# a state register read only by comparisons with constants (one-hot for
# `auto`) and builds new flip-flops whose power-up values include codes that
# are no value of the register, so the netlist was not the design from every
# power-up (txtask-v2 review, section 12, F2). Without it a state register
# keeps its own flip-flops, one per bit, as every other register does.
#
# `dfflegalize -cell $_DFF_P_ x`: every flip-flop becomes the plain rising-edge
# D flip-flop with NO initial value (contract C1: synchronous active-high reset,
# no initial values). Synchronous reset and clock enable stop being absorbed
# into a flop cell and become gates that ABC sees and the GE table prices: the
# sky130_fd_sc_hd library has no synchronous-reset flop, so this is what a
# sky130 mapping builds too (dfxtp_1 plus logic). An initialized flop ("x" =
# no init allowed) and an asynchronous reset (no $_DFF_PN0_ in the cell set)
# are Yosys ERRORS: the design is not scored. `abc` runs WITHOUT `-dff`
# (retiming would change the register structure that the proof is about).
#
# Area: gates and flops weighted by ge_seq.json. Depth: `ltp -noff`, which
# excludes the flops from the graph, so it is the number of gates on the
# longest combinational path between any two of {input port, flop Q, flop D,
# output port}: the clock-period proxy.
#
# `opt_clean -purge` (decided 2026-11-07; the combinational flow keeps plain
# `opt_clean`): the last clean-up also removes internal nets that have a
# public name (Yosys 0.53, `help opt_clean`), among them the dead
# public-named wires of techmapped cells (`\_269_.B`) with undriven bits,
# which the post-synthesis lint (check/postsynth.py, Verilator -Wall,
# UNDRIVEN fatal) refused in correct designs (tasks/arbiter/README.md, F6).
# It removes wires, never a cell or a port: the gate count, the GE and the
# depth are those of plain `opt_clean`.
read_rtlil @RTLIL@
synth -flatten -nofsm -top @TOP@
dfflegalize -cell $_DFF_P_ x
abc -g AND,NAND,OR,NOR,XOR,XNOR,ANDNOT,ORNOT,MUX
opt_clean -purge
tee -q -o @STAT@ stat -json
tee -q -o @LTP@ ltp -noff
write_verilog -noattr -noexpr @NETLIST@
